{
  "version": 1,
  "status": "approved",
  "about": [
    "Approved lettering geometry. See design/lettering-slots.md.",
    "",
    "Every box is a fraction of the panel, so one convention serves any panel size.",
    "A slot is a maximum box with an anchor, not a fixed rectangle: scripts/letterpress.py",
    "measures the text with the Helvetica metrics in scripts/textimage.py and shrinks the",
    "box to its content, growing away from the anchored corner.",
    "",
    "`order` is the placement convention. The first caption in a panel takes the first",
    "slot in the caption order, the second takes the next, and so on. The order is strict",
    "raster order so reading sequence is never ambiguous, which design/lettering.md requires.",
    "",
    "Dialogue is deliberately absent. A balloon needs a speaker position, which no",
    "convention can derive from a script; those 66 panels stay a manual pass.",
    "",
    "`top` and `bottom` are alternatives to the corner slots, never used alongside",
    "them; every other pair of slots is disjoint, which scripts/letterpress.py checks."
  ],
  "margin": 0.04,
  "padding": 0.014,
  "order": {
    "caption": [
      "tl",
      "tr",
      "bl",
      "br"
    ],
    "machine": [
      "block-r",
      "block-l"
    ],
    "interface": [
      "block-r",
      "block-l"
    ],
    "slate": [
